			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">/ooc The RL person behind Leadaer is having browser problems and asked me to post this story for him.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The story behind Leadaer’s past is one raveled in a shroud of mystery, as is most Scouts’. Why he decided become a Scout of Tunare, and not a ranger is probably related to a horrible time in his childhood. He had two loving parents, his father a ranger named Leadaer, as was his name. His mother, Dianu, did not focus herself to having the status of a druid, but still practiced healing. When he was only ten years old, Leadaer ventured into the Faydark, thinking he was going to become a ranger like his father, so thought he should get used to what his father did. He saw a rabbit, and tried to track it, but to no avail. His parents were terribly worried, for they didn’t know where he had gone. The left their house high in the trees, and asked the patrolling guards if they saw him. They all said he ran out into the forest, saying he was going to be just like his father. Leadaer began back toward Kelethin, and then he heard rustling, and disgusting chomping noises. He looked through the bushes to investigate, and he saw orcs, eating the rabbit he was tracking. He looked up at their grotesquely ugly faces, and the orcs look in his direction, and saw the discolored green of his tunic in the bushes. The orc was too stupid to realize this was out of place however, but Leadaer thought he did, so he ran. Then the orcs saw him sprinting through the forest, and began to chase him. His parents weren’t far away, and they heard his screams for help. His father ran quickly in that direction, hearing the battle cries of the orcs. Leadaer’s mother quickly followed. They found him, trying to back away from the orcs on the ground. Leadaer’s father was enraged, and quickly took out and fired an arrow from his Trueshot Longbow. The arrow flew straight at one of the orcs, and hit it squarely between the eyes. Then, Dianu blasted away an orc with an intense gust of wind, but there were still many orcs left. The orcs threw their weapons at Leadaer’s parents, and the elves dodged them. The orcs went into a battle frenzy, and charged at Leadaer and Dianu, bearing their teeth and claws. The child watched in horror as the orcs fought his parents, and they were winning. As they lay on ground, wounded beyond healing, the orcs stopped, and their eyes opened wide. Then, the orcs all fell to the ground, with stab marks in their backs, and there stood three rogues, Scouts of Tunare. He ran to his dying parents, and they whispered something to him with their last breaths. They suddenly went limp, and a ghostly white. Leadaer screamed up into the sky, and in his anguish, looked over to the rogues. Two of them had left, with one standing there, stone faced, but feeling pity for the child. Leadaer looked up at him, tears still in his eyes, and the rogue nodded at him. It is said that Leadaer followed the rogue, and the rogue helped him through his life, in the place his parents would have. Nonetheless, Leadaer chose to live the life of a scout, always destined to feel the pain of his parents’ deaths. Because of the tragic happenings, Leadaer now truly hates orcs, and kills them upon sight. He regards most indifferently, but he tends not to trust some.  
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />The good thing about repeating your mistakes is that you know when to duck.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
